{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxkfXjNioZVKfhxv7VbfWM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# KidSafe\n     2→\n     3→Lightweight parental control kiosk for macOS. Locks a user account to Firefox-only browsing with content filtering, time limits, and a parent dashboard.\n     4→\n     5→Single Python file, zero dependencies — just macOS and Firefox.\n     6→\n     7→## Features\n     8→\n     9→- **Firefox kiosk mode** — fullscreen, no browser chrome\n    10→- **Content filtering** — DNS-over-HTTPS via CleanBrowsing Family filter\n    11→- **Website whitelist** — only approved sites accessible (configurable)\n    12→- **Daily time limits** — with warnings and schedule (e.g. 7am–8pm)\n    13→- **Activity logging** — tracks sessions and usage in SQLite\n    14→- **Parent dashboard** — web UI at `http://127.0.0.1:8484` to manage settings, view usage, and control the kiosk\n    15→- **Auto-start on login** — LaunchAgent starts the kiosk when the child logs in\n    16→- **MDM profile** — optional `.mobileconfig` to restrict the Dock and hide System Preferences\n    17→\n    18→## Requirements\n    19→\n    20→- macOS 11+ (Big Sur or later)\n    21→- Python 3.8+ (included with macOS / Xcode CLI tools)\n    22→- Firefox installed in `/Applications/`\n    23→- A separate macOS user account for the child\n    24→\n    25→## Install\n    26→\n    27→```bash\n    28→curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tonycodes/kidsafe/main/install.sh | sudo bash -s -- <child_username>\n    29→```\n    30→\n    31→For example:\n    32→\n    33→```bash\n    34→curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tonycodes/kidsafe/main/install.sh | sudo bash -s -- emilio\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→You'll be prompted for a parent dashboard password. That's it — everything else is configured automatically:\n    38→\n    39→1. Downloads KidSafe to `/usr/local/kidsafe/`\n    40→2. Creates a `kidsafe` symlink in `/usr/local/bin/`\n    41→3. Sets up LaunchAgents for auto-start on login\n    42→4. Applies Firefox enterprise policies (DNS filtering, locked settings)\n    43→5. Configures the kiosk (120 min daily limit, 7am–8pm schedule)\n    44→\n    45→To re-run setup later or change settings interactively:\n    46→\n    47→```bash\n    48→kidsafe setup\n    49→```\n    50→\n    51→## Usage\n    52→\n    53→```bash\n    54→# Start the kiosk + dashboard\n    55→sudo -u <child_username> kidsafe start\n    56→\n    57→# Check status\n    58→kidsafe status\n    59→\n    60→# Stop the kiosk\n    61→kidsafe stop\n    62→\n    63→# Reset today's time usage\n    64→kidsafe reset\n    65→\n    66→# Re-apply Firefox policies after config changes\n    67→sudo kidsafe policies\n    68→```\n    69→\n    70→The kiosk starts automatically when the child logs in (via LaunchAgent). The parent dashboard is available at:\n    71→\n    72→```\n    73→http://127.0.0.1:8484\n    74→```\n    75→\n    76→## Parent Dashboard\n    77→\n    78→The dashboard lets you:\n    79→\n    80→- View remaining time and usage stats\n    81→- Adjust daily time limit and schedule\n    82→- Change the homepage\n    83→- Add/remove allowed websites\n    84→- View activity history and events\n    85→- Reset time or stop the kiosk remotely\n    86→\n    87→## Configuration\n    88→\n    89→Config is stored at `~/.kidsafe/config.json` (in the child's home directory). Key settings:\n    90→\n    91→| Setting | Default | Description |\n    92→|---------|---------|-------------|\n    93→| `daily_limit_minutes` | 120 | Max screen time per day |\n    94→| `schedule.allowed_start` | 07:00 | Earliest allowed time |\n    95→| `schedule.allowed_end` | 20:00 | Latest allowed time |\n    96→| `homepage` | youtube.com/kids | Browser start page |\n    97→| `allowed_sites` | 17 kid-safe sites | Whitelist of allowed domains |\n    98→| `dns_provider` | cleanbrowsing | DNS-over-HTTPS provider |\n    99→| `admin_port` | 8484 | Dashboard port |\n   100→\n   101→## How It Works\n   102→\n   103→- **Firefox Enterprise Policies** — written to `/Applications/Firefox.app/Contents/Resources/distribution/policies.json`. Forces DNS-over-HTTPS with CleanBrowsing Family filter, disables developer tools, private browsing, and about:config. Locks all settings so they can't be changed in Firefox.\n   104→- **Kiosk Mode** — Firefox launches with `--kiosk` flag (fullscreen, no URL bar, no tabs).\n   105→- **Website Filter** — Firefox's built-in `WebsiteFilter` policy blocks all sites except those in the whitelist.\n   106→- **Time Tracking** — usage tracked per-second in SQLite, enforced with configurable daily limits and time-of-day schedule.\n   107→- **LaunchAgent** — `com.kidsafe.kiosk.plist` runs at login with `KeepAlive` so Firefox restarts if closed.\n   108→\n   109→## Uninstall\n   110→\n   111→```bash\n   112→curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tonycodes/kidsafe/main/uninstall.sh | sudo bash\n   113→```\n   114→\n   115→Or if installed locally:\n   116→\n   117→```bash\n   118→sudo bash /usr/local/kidsafe/uninstall.sh\n   119→```\n   120→\n   121→This removes the app, LaunchAgents, Firefox policies, and any installed MDM profile. Config and logs in `~/.kidsafe/` are preserved — delete manually if needed.\n   122→\n   123→## License\n   124→\n   125→MIT\n   126→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS7mLKx1WRxatd7m3Xq9rh","session_id":"5f02eaca-ad87-4794-81b5-499b307ad8d6","uuid":"dbbeda32-cb25-4baf-b54a-11c92de314cf"}
