{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS7mLKx1WRxatd7m3Xq9rh","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding. Let me create a comprehensive report.\n\n## KidSafe Project Structure & Analysis\n\nI've completed a thorough exploration of the kidsafe project. Here's a comprehensive breakdown:\n\n### **1. Project Overview**\n\nKidSafe is a **lightweight parental control kiosk system for macOS** (1,152 lines, single Python file, zero dependencies). It locks a macOS user account to Firefox-only browsing with content filtering, time limits, and a parent web dashboard.\n\n**Key Technologies:**\n- Python 3.8+ (typed with mypy --strict)\n- SQLite3 for activity tracking\n- HTTP server (BaseHTTPRequestHandler) for parent dashboard\n- Firefox enterprise policies for content filtering\n- macOS LaunchAgent for auto-start\n\n---\n\n### **2. Project Structure**\n\n```\n/Users/tony/docker-dev/projects/kidsafe/\n├── kidsafe.py                 # Main application (1,152 lines)\n├── install.sh                 # Installer script (299 lines)\n├── uninstall.sh              # Uninstaller (referenced, not shown)\n├── kidsafe.mobileconfig      # MDM profile for Dock restrictions\n├── README.md                 # Documentation\n├── mypy.ini                  # Strict type checking config\n├── py.typed                  # PEP 561 marker for type stubs\n└── .gitignore\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. SQLite Database Setup**\n\n**Location:** `~/.kidsafe/activity.db`\n\n**3 Tables:**\n\n#### `sessions` (line 104-111)\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    start_time TEXT NOT NULL,\n    end_time TEXT,\n    duration_seconds INTEGER DEFAULT 0\n)\n```\n*Status: Defined but not actively used in current code (legacy table)*\n\n#### `daily_usage` (line 112-117)\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS daily_usage (\n    date TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    total_seconds INTEGER DEFAULT 0\n)\n```\n*Used to track total screen time per day (YYYY-MM-DD format)*\n\n#### `events` (line 118-125)\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS events (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    timestamp TEXT NOT NULL,\n    event_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n    detail TEXT\n)\n```\n*Activity log: firefox_start, firefox_stop, time_limit_reached, policy_update, app_blocked, kiosk_start, kiosk_stop, config_update, time_reset, outside_schedule*\n\n**Database Functions (lines 100-200):**\n- `init_db()` - Creates tables on startup\n- `record_event(event_type, detail)` - Log events to database\n- `get_today_usage()` - Total seconds used today\n- `update_daily_usage(seconds)` - Update today's total\n- `get_usage_history(days=7)` - Last N days usage\n- `get_recent_events(limit=50)` - Recent event list\n\n---\n\n### **4. API Endpoints**\n\n**Port:** 8484 (configurable, default)  \n**Handler Class:** `DashboardHandler` (lines 862-955)\n\n#### **GET Endpoints (require auth token)**\n\n| Endpoint | Returns | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|---------|\n| `/` or `/dashboard` | HTML | Serve dashboard UI |\n| `/api/status` | JSON | `{used_minutes, remaining_minutes, limit_minutes, firefox_running, within_schedule}` |\n| `/api/config` | JSON | Configuration without password hash |\n| `/api/history` | JSON | `[{date, minutes}, ...]` (7-day history) |\n| `/api/events` | JSON | `[{time, type, detail}, ...]` (50 most recent) |\n\n#### **POST Endpoints**\n\n| Endpoint | Purpose | Auth | Returns |\n|----------|---------|------|---------|\n| `/api/login` | Authenticate | None (password-based) | `{token: \"...\"}` or error |\n| `/api/config` | Update config | Token | `{ok: true}` |\n| `/api/reset-time` | Reset daily usage to 0 | Token | `{ok: true}` |\n| `/api/apply-policies` | Apply Firefox policies | Token | `{ok, message}` |\n| `/api/stop-kiosk` | Stop the kiosk | Token | `{ok: true}` |\n\n**Authentication:**\n- Password hashed with SHA256 (salt + password)\n- Token: 64-char hex string (secrets.token_hex(32))\n- Tokens stored in memory during session (not persisted)\n\n---\n\n### **5. Parent Dashboard Implementation**\n\n**File:** Embedded in `kidsafe.py` as `DASHBOARD_HTML` string (lines 667-859)\n\n**Frontend Stack:**\n- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript (no framework)\n- Apple-system font, macOS design aesthetic\n- Real-time refresh: `setInterval(render, 30000)` (30 seconds)\n\n**Sections:**\n\n1. **Login** (lines 734-743)\n   - Password input → `/api/login` POST\n   - Token stored in sessionStorage\n\n2. **Status Dashboard** (lines 759-764)\n   - Minutes left today\n   - Minutes used (progress bar with color coding)\n   - Firefox running status\n\n3. **Settings** (lines 766-785)\n   - Daily time limit (number input)\n   - Schedule (start/end times)\n   - Homepage URL\n\n4. **Allowed Sites** (lines 787-794)\n   - Tag list of allowed domains\n   - Add/remove buttons\n   - Inline site editor\n\n5. **Usage History** (lines 796-801)\n   - 7-day table: date vs minutes used\n\n6. **Recent Activity** (lines 803-808)\n   - Event log: timestamp, event type, detail\n   - Color-coded event types (firefox_start=green, firefox_stop=red, etc.)\n\n7. **Controls** (lines 810-815)\n   - Reset today's time button\n   - Apply Firefox policies button\n   - Danger: Stop kiosk button\n\n**JavaScript Functions:**\n- `api(path, method, body)` - Fetch wrapper with auth token\n- `login(password)` - `/api/login` POST\n- `saveLimit()`, `saveSchedule()`, `saveHomepage()` - Config updates\n- `addSite()`, `removeSite()` - Manage whitelist\n- `resetTime()`, `applyPolicies()`, `stopKiosk()` - Control functions\n\n---\n\n### **6. Kiosk Manager Implementation**\n\n**Class:** `KioskManager` (lines 453-663)\n\n**Key Methods:**\n\n| Method | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `launch_firefox()` | Start Firefox with `--kiosk` flag |\n| `stop_firefox()` | Terminate Firefox process |\n| `is_firefox_running()` | Check if process alive |\n| `is_within_schedule()` | Compare current time to allowed window (07:00-20:00) |\n| `get_remaining_minutes()` | Calculate time left today |\n| `ensure_firefox_fullscreen()` | Send Cmd+Shift+F if not fullscreen |\n| `show_notification()` | macOS notification via osascript |\n| `show_times_up_screen()` | Dialog when daily limit reached |\n| `show_outside_schedule_screen()` | Dialog outside allowed hours |\n| `run()` | Main loop (lines 590-658) |\n\n**Main Loop (`run()` - lines 590-658):**\n1. Check if within schedule → if not, wait and show dialog\n2. Check daily usage vs limit → if over, stop Firefox and show \"time's up\" dialog\n3. Show warning notification (10 min before limit by default)\n4. Launch Firefox if not running\n5. Ensure Firefox fullscreen every 5 seconds\n6. Update daily usage (increment by 1 second every second)\n7. Sleep 1 second, repeat\n\n**Firefox Policies (lines 248-348):**\n- **DNSOverHTTPS**: CleanBrowsing Family filter (forced)\n- **BlockAboutConfig**, **BlockAboutProfiles**, **BlockAboutAddons**: Disable dangerous pages\n- **DisableDeveloperTools**, **DisablePrivateBrowsing**, **DisableProfileImport**\n- **WebsiteFilter**: Whitelist mode → block all except allowed_sites\n- **ManagedBookmarks**: Auto-create toolbar bookmarks for allowed sites\n- Config written to `/Applications/Firefox.app/Contents/Resources/distribution/policies.json`\n\n---\n\n### **7. App Enforcer (Kiosk Security)**\n\n**Class:** `AppEnforcer` (lines 422-449)\n\n**Purpose:** Kill any GUI app not in the whitelist (background thread)\n\n**Allowed Apps:**\n```python\nALLOWED_APP_BUNDLES = {\"firefox.app\"}\n```\n\n**Methods:**\n- `find_unauthorized_apps()` - Parse `ps -eo pid,comm` output\n- `kill_unauthorized_apps()` - SIGKILL any non-whitelisted .app\n- `start()` - Launch background enforcer thread\n- `stop()` - Stop enforcer\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Runs `ps -eo pid,comm` every 2 seconds\n2. Searches for `/Applications/` in process command\n3. Extracts .app name using regex: `r\"/([^/]+\\.app)/\"`\n4. Sends SIGKILL to any non-whitelisted app (except firefox.app)\n5. Records blocked app as event\n\n---\n\n### **8. Configuration Management**\n\n**Location:** `~/.kidsafe/config.json` (JSON file)\n\n**Default Config (lines 43-83):**\n```json\n{\n  \"child_user\": \"emilio\",\n  \"admin_password_hash\": \"\",\n  \"admin_port\": 8484,\n  \"daily_limit_minutes\": 120,\n  \"warning_minutes\": 10,\n  \"schedule\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"allowed_start\": \"07:00\",\n    \"allowed_end\": \"20:00\"\n  },\n  \"firefox_kiosk\": true,\n  \"homepage\": \"https://www.youtube.com/kids\",\n  \"allowed_sites\": [\n    \"youtube.com\", \"youtu.be\", \"pbskids.org\", \"nickjr.com\",\n    \"disney.com\", \"disneyplus.com\", \"netflix.com\", \"khanacademy.org\",\n    \"abcya.com\", \"coolmathgames.com\", \"nationalgeographic.com/kids\",\n    \"funbrain.com\", \"starfall.com\", \"typingclub.com\", \"scratch.mit.edu\",\n    \"code.org\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_sites\": [],\n  \"dns_provider\": \"cleanbrowsing\",\n  \"dns_providers\": {\n    \"cleanbrowsing\": \"https://doh.cleanbrowsing.org/doh/family-filter/\",\n    \"cloudflare_family\": \"https://family.cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query\",\n    \"opendns\": \"https://doh.familyshield.opendns.com/dns-query\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Functions:**\n- `load_config()` - Load from file, merge with defaults\n- `save_config(config)` - Write to JSON file\n- `hash_password(password)` - SHA256 with 16-byte salt\n- `verify_password(password, stored)` - Constant-time comparison\n\n---\n\n### **9. CLI Commands**\n\n**Main Entry:** `kidsafe <command>` (lines 1119-1152)\n\n| Command | Implementation | Purpose |\n|---------|-----------------|---------|\n| `setup` | `cmd_setup()` | Interactive config wizard (supports flags: --child, --password, --password-env, --limit, --homepage) |\n| `start` | `cmd_start()` | Start kiosk + dashboard (launches dashboard in background thread) |\n| `stop` | `cmd_stop()` | Kill kiosk process via pgrep + SIGTERM |\n| `status` | `cmd_status()` | Print current status to stdout |\n| `reset` | `cmd_reset()` | Reset daily usage to 0 |\n| `policies` | `cmd_policies()` | Apply Firefox policies |\n\n---\n\n### **10. Installation & Setup**\n\n**Install Script:** `install.sh` (299 lines)\n\n**Installation Flow:**\n1. Pre-flight checks (root, macOS, Python 3, child user exists, Firefox installed)\n2. Stop old instance\n3. Download/copy files to `/usr/local/kidsafe/`\n4. Create symlink: `/usr/local/bin/kidsafe`\n5. Create LaunchAgent for child: `com.kidsafe.kiosk.plist` (auto-start on login)\n6. Create LaunchAgent for admin: `com.kidsafe.dashboard.plist` (optional)\n7. Prompt for admin password\n8. Initialize config.json + activity.db\n9. Apply Firefox policies\n10. Start kiosk\n\n**Auto-start via LaunchAgent:**\n```xml\n<key>ProgramArguments</key>\n<array>\n  <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>\n  <string>/usr/local/kidsafe/kidsafe.py</string>\n  <string>start</string>\n</array>\n<key>KeepAlive</key>\n<true/>  <!-- Restart if Firefox closes -->\n```\n\n---\n\n### **11. Key Files & File Paths**\n\n| Component | Location | Description |\n|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| Main app | `/usr/local/kidsafe/kidsafe.py` | Single-file implementation |\n| Config | `~/.kidsafe/config.json` | JSON configuration |\n| Database | `~/.kidsafe/activity.db` | SQLite activity log |\n| Logs | `~/.kidsafe/kidsafe.log` | Text log file |\n| Firefox policies | `/Applications/Firefox.app/Contents/Resources/distribution/policies.json` | Enterprise policies |\n| LaunchAgent (child) | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kidsafe.kiosk.plist` | Auto-start kiosk |\n| LaunchAgent (admin) | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kidsafe.dashboard.plist` | Optional admin launcher |\n| Stdout/Stderr | `~/.kidsafe/stdout.log`, `~/.kidsafe/stderr.log` | LaunchAgent output |\n\n---\n\n### **12. Type Hints & Code Quality**\n\n**Strict Typing (mypy.ini):**\n- `strict = True` - Full type checking enabled\n- `disallow_untyped_defs = True` - All functions must be typed\n- Recent fixes (commit 9a947d8): Resolved mypy --strict errors\n\n**Type Annotations Throughout:**\n- All functions have complete type signatures\n- Uses `typing` module: `Dict`, `List`, `Optional`, `Set`, `Any`\n- Type hints on class attributes (e.g., `firefox_process: Optional[subprocess.Popen[bytes]]`)\n\n---\n\n### **13. Security Architecture**\n\n| Layer | Mechanism |\n|-------|-----------|\n| **Authentication** | SHA256 password hash + session tokens |\n| **Firefox Content** | DNS-over-HTTPS + WebsiteFilter policy |\n| **App Whitelisting** | Continuous process monitoring (AppEnforcer) |\n| **Time Enforcement** | Daemon loop with per-second tracking |\n| **Schedule** | Time-of-day enforcement |\n| **Policy Lock** | Firefox enterprise policies (can't be disabled by user) |\n\n---\n\n### **Summary of Key Patterns**\n\n1. **Database**: 3 tables (sessions, daily_usage, events) - pure activity logging, no browsing history\n2. **API**: RESTful JSON endpoints, token-based auth, all return JSON\n3. **Dashboard**: Single HTML file, vanilla JS, 30-second auto-refresh\n4. **Kiosk**: Background loop checking schedule/limits, launching/monitoring Firefox\n5. **App Enforcer**: Background thread using `ps` command (no special permissions needed)\n6. **Firefox Control**: Enterprise policies JSON + process management\n7. **Config**: Single JSON file, loaded on startup, merged with defaults\n8. **CLI**: 6 commands with subcommand-style arguments\n\nThis is a well-architected, production-ready parental control system with clean separation of concerns between the kiosk manager, app enforcer, dashboard server, and configuration system."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a7491e5369268ea17 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 97668\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 59558</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f02eaca-ad87-4794-81b5-499b307ad8d6","uuid":"428b4845-eced-443c-b399-288fd46bf22d","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore th